  "drivers": "Stocks are lower across the board as investors brace for a pivotal AI week: Nvidia reports Q3 results Tuesday, its first since Jensen Huang resigned last Thursday, and Anthropic is expected to price a record IPO on Thursday (targeting ~$1.4T valuation). Nvidia hit session lows after a CNBC report that its board is not considering reinstating Huang, despite an FT report of a campaign to bring him back and President Trump publicly backing the idea. Chips are the epicenter (SOXX −4.6%, MU −6.5%, INTC −6.5% on a shareholder class action, SNDK −7.3%), with Vanda Research warning Anthropic's debut could pull money from other AI names; crypto stocks slide with Bitcoin near $64.8K. Defensive staples (TSN, CPB, GIS) and managed care (MOH, CNC) are bid. Oil is down ~2.8% as Strait of Hormuz shipments recover; the NY Fed manufacturing index fell to 7.8 in November from 25.5.",
